Tables: StdFtStorBytes(ft) for a plain near-contract-standards FT and
StdWNearStorBytes(wnear) for wNEAR; the parameter is the token's model
account (measured on ft-probe.near and wnear-probe.near).  Keys as in
CalibStd: <acct>.<method>/<path> where the bytes depend on the path
(storage_deposit and near_deposit /new and /registered; no method key,
since the paths differ), else <acct>.<method>.  size: the holder's
account id length in bytes (storage_deposit's account_id; the caller
for near_deposit and storage_unregister).  A registration is 1 (prefix)
+ 4 + len(id) + 16 (u128) + 40 = 61 + len(id) bytes, Nep145's
StdRegBytes; storage_unregister (no balance left) frees as many;
transfers and withdrawals overwrite balances in place, 0 bytes.
Probe contracts built with --cfg near (probes/build.sh).
